    "author_association": "NONE",
    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\r\n\r\n- [X] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\r\n- [X] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\r\n- [X] I have updated 'mini.nvim' to latest version\r\n\r\n### Module(s)\r\n\r\nmini.files\r\n\r\n### Description\r\n\r\nFirst, thanks for amazing plugin. I've been enjoying this plugin so much! The issue is:\r\n\r\nWhen I go in to the file inside mini.files and there's a swap alert, after I respond to swap alert I'm seeing this error:\r\n\r\n<img width=\"1387\" alt=\"Screenshot 2023-07-10 at 5 43 03 AM\" src=\"https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/assets/12246126/c2db7abb-15aa-4bb1-a420-4d6a50be3307\">\r\n\r\nThis is not that annoying for regular go in. But for go_in_plus (key L) which closes the mini.files window when I go inside the file, this error actually prevent the closing of the mini.files window.\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n### Neovim version\r\n\r\n760c1f3619418f769526884a3de47f0b76245887 (top of tree)\r\n\r\n### Steps to reproduce\r\n\r\n1. Setup mini.files with default setting\r\n2. Go in plus to file with swap using key 'L'\r\n3. Error shows up and the mini.files window does not close\r\n\r\n\r\n### Expected behavior\r\n\r\nNo error and mini.files window closes\r\n\r\n### Actual behavior\r\n\r\nError shows up and mini.files window does not close",
